WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.842
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:07.112 --> 00:08.864
[theme music playing]

3
00:46.694 --> 00:50.739
A LOVE OTHER THAN YOURS

4
00:50.865 --> 00:52.491
[theme music concludes]

5
00:52.616 --> 00:53.450
ALL PERSONS, LOCATIONS, RELIGIONS, INCIDENTS, AND ORGANIZATIONS IN THIS DRAMA

6
00:53.576 --> 00:54.410
ARE FICTITIOUS

7
00:54.535 --> 00:55.369
CHILD ACTORS HAVE FILMED SAFELY UNDER PARENTAL SUPERVISION

8
00:55.494 --> 00:56.370
SCENES INVOLVING ANIMALS WERE FILMED SAFELY WITH EXPERT ADVICE AND COOPERATION

9
00:56.495 --> 00:57.913
[downbeat music playing]

10
01:10.301 --> 01:12.261
[exhales deeply]

11
01:16.098 --> 01:17.057
How about breakfast?

12
01:18.142 --> 01:19.810
Since fate brought us together.

13
01:20.519 --> 01:22.229
I brought something for a hangover.

14
01:33.657 --> 01:34.491
[exhales sharply]

15
01:46.587 --> 01:47.755
[phone vibrates]

16
01:49.131 --> 01:50.758
[woman] Bambi is just so incredibly cute.

17
01:50.883 --> 01:51.800
Has she been adopted?

18
01:57.014 --> 01:58.557
[downbeat music concludes]

19
01:59.016 --> 01:59.975
Tell me, how does it taste?

20
02:02.061 --> 02:03.604
Uh, good.

21
02:07.232 --> 02:09.985
-Hey, last night-- -He's a real pain when he's drunk, right?

22
02:12.154 --> 02:14.490
He clings to you, then suddenly passes out,

23
02:15.616 --> 02:17.868
and he won't wake up from anything, right?

24
02:17.993 --> 02:19.078
Hey.

25
02:19.578 --> 02:20.537
What do you see in him?

26
02:20.663 --> 02:22.831
[chokes, coughs]

27
02:28.879 --> 02:30.214
Su-a, let's go. I'll take you home.

28
02:32.091 --> 02:33.092
Because he's extraordinary.

29
02:36.053 --> 02:37.471
To me, Namgung is…

30
02:40.641 --> 02:42.851
He's the best person I've ever met.

31
02:47.189 --> 02:48.774
[emotional music playing]

32
02:48.899 --> 02:51.193
[breathes deeply]

33
03:04.707 --> 03:05.874
[exhales deeply]

34
03:06.000 --> 03:08.127
[liquid pouring]

35
03:18.053 --> 03:20.889
[breathing heavily]

36
03:28.605 --> 03:29.732
[emotional music concludes]

37
03:29.857 --> 03:30.941
Are you angry?

38
03:31.525 --> 03:32.609
You should be the angry one.

39
03:34.028 --> 03:36.447
My ex forced her way into my home while you were there.

40
03:36.822 --> 03:39.616
You should have kicked my shins not eaten breakfast with us.

41
03:40.701 --> 03:42.578
I didn't want to make it harder for you.

42
03:43.412 --> 03:45.164
She would have gotten the wrong idea.

43
03:46.498 --> 03:47.332
Come on.

44
03:48.333 --> 03:49.710
We were fully dressed, right?

45
03:49.835 --> 03:50.711
When I'm drunk,

46
03:50.836 --> 03:53.756
the only thing I do is sleep like a baby for six whole hours.

47
03:54.381 --> 03:55.924
Mi-do knows better than anyone.

48
03:56.842 --> 03:57.926
That's not true.

49
04:00.429 --> 04:01.764
Something happened between us.

50
04:02.473 --> 04:03.557
[light music playing]

51
04:08.228 --> 04:09.229
[scoffs]

52
04:10.647 --> 04:11.899
Your acting's gotten really good.

53
04:12.024 --> 04:13.525
I almost believed you.

54
04:14.818 --> 04:16.320
Thanks for seeing me home.

55
04:19.656 --> 04:22.493
Hey, don't joke about stuff like that.

56
04:23.827 --> 04:27.081
Now that I think of it, your door lock passcode

57
04:27.206 --> 04:29.625
being your ex's birthday is really annoying.

58
04:45.390 --> 04:46.266
[sighs]

59
04:46.391 --> 04:47.267
[light music concludes]

60
04:55.109 --> 04:56.360
[door keypad beeps]

61
04:57.611 --> 04:59.154
Hey, we're here.

62
04:59.279 --> 05:00.989
Got you. Got you. Okay.

63
05:01.115 --> 05:02.074
[Namgung groans]

64
05:02.199 --> 05:03.659
[Su-a] Take your shoes off. Come on.

65
05:03.784 --> 05:05.160
-Take them off. -[Namgung] I don't wanna.

66
05:05.285 --> 05:06.411
[Su-a] Hold on. Hold on. Hold on.

67
05:06.537 --> 05:07.663
Almost there.

68
05:08.205 --> 05:09.540
Lie down here. Lie down here.

69
05:09.665 --> 05:11.500
Here you go. Easy. [groans]

70
05:12.209 --> 05:14.253
[pants]

71
05:15.504 --> 05:16.672
[groans]

72
05:19.424 --> 05:20.759
[grunts]

73
05:37.943 --> 05:39.361
[tender music playing]

74
05:40.988 --> 05:42.197
Mr. Namgung,

75
05:44.032 --> 05:46.285
I'm afraid I lied to you again.

76
05:47.786 --> 05:49.246
I want to make you happy.

77
05:51.248 --> 05:52.666
Every single second.

78
05:54.877 --> 05:55.961
While we're dating.

79
05:58.380 --> 06:01.091
Not just for a second, like I said before.

80
06:03.677 --> 06:05.262
That's my one and only goal.

81
06:09.057 --> 06:11.059
I'll only stay for ten minutes.

82
06:13.187 --> 06:14.771
Ten minutes is okay, right?

83
06:28.577 --> 06:30.329
[door keypad beeps]

84
06:30.454 --> 06:31.455
[door opens]

85
06:35.167 --> 06:36.418
[door lock chimes]

86
06:40.130 --> 06:41.340
We need to talk.

87
06:41.465 --> 06:43.050
We're broken up right now.

88
06:44.009 --> 06:45.093
You don't have to apologize.

89
06:45.219 --> 06:46.762
I'm not apologizing.

90
06:50.349 --> 06:51.433
Switch up your door code.

91
06:52.142 --> 06:53.185
I'll change mine too.

92
06:54.519 --> 06:55.520
And for the time left,

93
06:55.938 --> 06:57.856
let's not visit the place of the other.

94
07:03.779 --> 07:04.696
I'll change it.

95
07:05.948 --> 07:07.532
If you're done, please leave now.

96
07:08.116 --> 07:11.453
I don't want us visiting each other from this moment on.

97
07:12.621 --> 07:15.249
I felt terrible until I took Su-a home.

98
07:17.125 --> 07:20.963
But on the way back home, something crossed my mind.

99
07:23.799 --> 07:25.509
"Is this what she wanted?"

100
07:29.513 --> 07:30.722
You wanted pain, right?

101
07:31.765 --> 07:32.641
How does it feel?

102
07:35.269 --> 07:36.144
Like shit.

103
07:38.063 --> 07:39.147
Disgusting.

104
07:41.942 --> 07:42.776
And you?

105
07:43.777 --> 07:44.903
Do you feel good?

106
07:46.113 --> 07:47.030
No.

107
07:48.573 --> 07:49.491
Feels like shit.

108
07:52.536 --> 07:53.453
Disgusting.

109
08:01.712 --> 08:05.590
A LOVE OTHER THAN YOURS

110
08:05.716 --> 08:11.596
HOW DO WE LOVE, HOW DO WE LIVE?

111
08:13.265 --> 08:14.558
[tender music concludes]

112
08:15.392 --> 08:16.935
[ambient music playing over speakers]

113
08:20.397 --> 08:22.316
-[phone vibrates] -[woman] Bambi is just so incredibly cute.

114
08:22.816 --> 08:24.067
Has she been adopted?

115
08:27.154 --> 08:28.405
[exhales deeply]

116
08:29.531 --> 08:31.825
BAMBI

117
08:31.950 --> 08:35.203
LOVABLE BAMBI IS LOOKING FOR A NEW FAMILY

118
08:50.177 --> 08:51.845
[phone camera clicking]

119
08:59.644 --> 09:00.812
Come on, smile a little.

120
09:02.564 --> 09:04.191
We break up in about ten days.

121
09:04.316 --> 09:05.150
Chin up.

122
09:06.234 --> 09:07.319
[sighs]

123
09:18.663 --> 09:19.581
Okay.

124
09:20.499 --> 09:21.416
I get it.

125
09:22.209 --> 09:23.668
I get that you can't leave Namgung.

126
09:24.419 --> 09:25.420
I can live with that.

127
09:28.173 --> 09:30.425
You still have to keep seeing me until our time is done.

128
09:31.009 --> 09:31.968
No take-backs.

129
09:33.011 --> 09:34.221
You could at least do that.

130
09:35.263 --> 09:36.848
It's not like it's exactly hard.

131
09:38.475 --> 09:40.769
You pulled some stunts behind my back. How would I do that?

132
09:42.813 --> 09:44.022
You dug into my past.

133
09:46.400 --> 09:47.442
No, I didn't.

134
09:50.487 --> 09:51.530
I swear I didn't.

135
09:52.406 --> 09:53.615
Except for looking into your past.

136
09:55.117 --> 09:55.951
That was it.

137
10:04.042 --> 10:05.001
And your meds.

138
10:06.378 --> 10:07.462
Are you taking them?

139
10:08.880 --> 10:10.257
Tell me, when did it start?

140
10:12.676 --> 10:14.177
I have sociopathic tendencies.

141
10:15.512 --> 10:17.055
Meds don't exactly cure that.

142
10:18.140 --> 10:19.182
It won't help with that.

143
10:19.558 --> 10:21.017
I didn't mean that and you know it.

144
10:25.021 --> 10:26.022
[groans]

145
10:27.607 --> 10:29.526
Please, can't you just pretend not to notice?

146
10:31.153 --> 10:32.154
[sighs softly]

147
10:32.279 --> 10:33.363
[scoffs]

148
10:40.287 --> 10:41.329
If I tell you about it…

149
10:44.374 --> 10:45.500
wanna sleep together?

150
10:47.294 --> 10:48.336
[soft music playing]

151
11:09.399 --> 11:14.070
Miss Lee, just in case you don't know, I'm not underage.

152
11:16.072 --> 11:17.824
[breathes deeply]

153
11:17.949 --> 11:19.993
And obviously you're not either.

154
11:21.119 --> 11:23.955
Two voting age adults don't need to be this innocent.

155
11:24.998 --> 11:27.000
This is why the fertility rate is low.

156
11:33.048 --> 11:34.049
[soft music concludes]

157
11:34.174 --> 11:37.010
No, no, wait, that was just… a joke.

158
11:38.178 --> 11:39.387
-[soft music resumes] -Okay?

159
11:41.848 --> 11:43.892
Just stay by me till I sleep, all right?

160
11:47.771 --> 11:48.897
Come on, sit down.

161
11:53.318 --> 11:54.361
[clears throat]

162
12:02.118 --> 12:03.453
[music swells]

163
12:05.747 --> 12:07.332
I think that all of this is because of you.

164
12:09.125 --> 12:11.628
It started four months ago out of nowhere.

165
12:14.172 --> 12:15.757
I can't find any other reason.

166
12:16.424 --> 12:17.968
Then you should have come to Ahyeon-dong.

167
12:19.636 --> 12:21.555
I remember they found you in Myeong-dong.

168
12:23.223 --> 12:25.058
I heard what the police said to you.

169
12:34.651 --> 12:36.152
In the time we have together…

170
12:38.363 --> 12:39.614
I'll look into it, okay?

171
12:41.449 --> 12:43.285
The reason you keep going to Myeong-dong,

172
12:44.035 --> 12:45.370
I'll look into that for you.

173
12:47.747 --> 12:48.582
Why?

174
12:50.917 --> 12:52.168
You pity me or what?

175
12:53.378 --> 12:57.132
Since you'll dump me soon? To relieve your guilt?

176
13:02.762 --> 13:03.930
It's not that.

177
13:05.724 --> 13:07.142
I can't bear to watch you hurt.

178
13:09.728 --> 13:12.105
I wish I could make your pain all go away.

179
13:21.531 --> 13:22.782
[soft music concludes]

180
13:28.121 --> 13:30.332
GEUMSEOK TEAHOUSE

181
13:40.258 --> 13:41.092
When did you start?

182
13:41.217 --> 13:42.177
Last September.

183
13:42.302 --> 13:44.220
So, you joined my team because…

184
13:44.346 --> 13:46.306
The sample dates, I needed them.

185
13:48.058 --> 13:49.392
Is that all you have to say?

186
13:51.603 --> 13:52.771
Sure, of course.

187
13:53.730 --> 13:55.565
For what other reason would I join?

188
13:57.275 --> 13:58.610
It could be because of a guy.

189
13:58.735 --> 13:59.903
[suspenseful music playing]

190
14:00.445 --> 14:02.822
A guy you've always dreamed of working with

191
14:02.947 --> 14:04.491
and watched with a racing heart.

192
14:12.082 --> 14:13.416
Just to work with a guy like me.

193
14:13.541 --> 14:15.418
-[playful music playing] -[chuckles]

194
14:17.212 --> 14:18.672
I knew it all along.

195
14:18.797 --> 14:21.841
An Hunmin Confectionery legend, the top recruit of the company,

196
14:21.966 --> 14:23.635
and Hot Chocolate Chips' youngest lead.

197
14:24.135 --> 14:26.596
So you chose me.

198
14:28.223 --> 14:29.140
I get it.

199
14:29.265 --> 14:30.433
[chuckles awkwardly]

200
14:30.558 --> 14:31.643
All right.

201
14:32.018 --> 14:35.021
Now that I've shown you my hand, please share what you've found.

202
14:35.522 --> 14:37.148
You think that's enough to get me to talk?

203
14:37.273 --> 14:40.402
Based on your time off, you only started investigating two months ago.

204
14:40.944 --> 14:44.531
You'd think you filmed the sweet potato swap or something.

205
14:48.201 --> 14:49.452
How did you know?

206
14:52.997 --> 14:54.332
I feel like I'm not enough.

207
14:55.959 --> 15:00.755
You started last year while I only needed two months to get the video done.

208
15:01.423 --> 15:03.758
Now you say why I'm the legend of Hun min.

209
15:04.759 --> 15:05.593
Um…

210
15:05.927 --> 15:07.345
Did you film it? Seriously?

211
15:09.222 --> 15:13.309
I have a plan, and I'll let you in on one condition.

212
15:15.061 --> 15:16.062
Namgung.

213
15:16.813 --> 15:18.022
Never trust that kid.

214
15:19.441 --> 15:20.483
[playful music concludes]

215
15:32.704 --> 15:33.788
Deok-sun,

216
15:34.706 --> 15:36.249
your fantasy is all wrong.

217
15:36.875 --> 15:38.918
A good man treats you to fine dining.

218
15:39.043 --> 15:40.462
He doesn't just cook for you.

219
15:41.921 --> 15:43.757
[Ho-sik] I thought you might misunderstand,

220
15:43.882 --> 15:45.467
so I'm telling you this now.

221
15:45.884 --> 15:47.886
That Namgung isn't on our side.

222
15:48.720 --> 15:50.472
He went to Procurement long ago.

223
15:51.014 --> 15:55.602
You see, Namgung stole my work phone while getting me completely wasted.

224
15:57.145 --> 16:01.357
All the footage is stored on it, so we have to find that phone.

225
16:01.858 --> 16:03.693
It's over at Namgung's apartment.

226
16:09.657 --> 16:10.909
I want some banana milk.

227
16:13.536 --> 16:15.872
I like having banana milk with my steak, you know?

228
16:23.797 --> 16:25.799
-[door lock chimes] -[upbeat music playing]

229
16:52.826 --> 16:53.827
[gasps]

230
16:55.453 --> 16:56.579
[music falls]

231
17:01.835 --> 17:02.919
[music rises]

232
17:21.396 --> 17:22.647
[door keypad beeps]

233
17:23.314 --> 17:24.941
[groans, yelps]

234
17:31.614 --> 17:32.866
[upbeat music concludes]

235
17:34.659 --> 17:35.618
[door lock chimes]

236
17:39.747 --> 17:42.959
Grease spluttered, and I love a clean space.

237
17:49.632 --> 17:50.842
Clean it all good.

238
17:57.849 --> 17:59.350
Did Ho-sik say to find his phone?

239
18:02.395 --> 18:03.855
Is that guy delusional?

240
18:04.439 --> 18:07.317
He lost it when he got drunk, so why treat me like a thief?

241
18:08.276 --> 18:10.987
That area's full of thieves who steal phones from everyone.

242
18:12.614 --> 18:15.199
That's probably in Thailand or Vietnam by now.

243
18:16.451 --> 18:17.410
That's right.

244
18:18.119 --> 18:19.495
He was mistaken, right?

245
18:21.331 --> 18:22.290
[laughs]

246
18:22.415 --> 18:24.250
I knew it wasn't true. [laughs]

247
18:24.834 --> 18:26.169
I never believed him.

248
18:26.294 --> 18:27.921
I just looked for it just in case.

249
18:28.588 --> 18:30.548
You and Procurement? No way.

250
18:31.466 --> 18:32.550
I did get an offer.

251
18:35.136 --> 18:37.680
I saw Jeong Yeon-ho rig the sugar test with my own eyes.

252
18:41.059 --> 18:44.771
I tried to ignore it, but they just won't move on.

253
18:48.524 --> 18:51.819
[Yeon-ho] There's an interesting line that Marlon Brando says

254
18:51.945 --> 18:53.029
in The Godfather.

255
18:53.154 --> 18:54.489
[mischievous music playing]

256
18:54.614 --> 18:59.160
Keep your friends close and your enemies closer.

257
19:01.454 --> 19:05.166
So in that spirit, and after much consideration,

258
19:05.708 --> 19:07.293
I have decided to take you under my wing.

259
19:07.877 --> 19:09.045
You really don't have to do it.

260
19:09.837 --> 19:10.672
What?

261
19:13.383 --> 19:14.759
I'll pretend I saw nothing.

262
19:14.884 --> 19:16.260
[sighs wearily]

263
19:18.346 --> 19:19.180
I mean it.

264
19:21.307 --> 19:22.475
I swear.

265
19:24.143 --> 19:25.645
Do I sound like I'm joking to you?

266
19:27.647 --> 19:29.315
Does it sound like I'm joking to you?

267
19:29.857 --> 19:31.734
Listen, I'm serious.

268
19:32.276 --> 19:34.654
I'm offering you a fantastic opportunity.

269
19:34.779 --> 19:37.073
You won't get anything like that ever. Don't you see?

270
19:37.198 --> 19:38.199
Opportunity?

271
19:38.908 --> 19:40.910
You screwed everything up, got caught,

272
19:41.035 --> 19:42.662
and now you're just trying to hide it.

273
19:42.787 --> 19:45.164
[chuckling]

274
19:45.707 --> 19:50.169
Of course, I admit anyone would want a talent like mine on their team.

275
19:50.294 --> 19:52.046
I'm afraid you have the wrong idea.

276
19:52.171 --> 19:53.631
This isn't about damage control.

277
19:53.756 --> 19:54.590
I was just asking--

278
19:54.716 --> 19:57.176
Marlon Brando didn't say it. It was Al Pacino.

279
19:57.301 --> 19:59.303
[gun cocks, fires]

280
19:59.429 --> 20:00.263
Huh?

281
20:00.388 --> 20:01.639
Keep your friends close…

282
20:03.683 --> 20:05.601
-and your enemies closer. -[mischievous music concludes]

283
20:05.727 --> 20:07.145
[Namgung] Al Pacino said that line.

284
20:08.271 --> 20:10.273
That's from The Godfather Part II.

285
20:10.398 --> 20:12.108
Marlon Brando dies in the first film.

286
20:14.360 --> 20:15.486
You haven't seen it.

287
20:16.362 --> 20:17.655
Spoiler. I'm sorry.

288
20:19.699 --> 20:21.034
That's not the issue right now.

289
20:22.118 --> 20:23.828
You declined their offer, right?

290
20:24.704 --> 20:25.580
No.

291
20:26.539 --> 20:27.582
I'm thinking about it.

292
20:28.374 --> 20:29.751
Honestly, I nearly gave in.

293
20:30.752 --> 20:33.588
For a guy with zero connections, those chances don't come often.

294
20:34.464 --> 20:37.050
The only reason I spent time with them was to test the waters.

295
20:42.430 --> 20:43.973
[gentle music playing]

296
20:44.849 --> 20:46.309
I don't think I can eat with you.

297
20:47.393 --> 20:48.478
I'll be going now.

298
20:59.530 --> 21:00.656
[door opens]

299
21:05.995 --> 21:07.038
[door lock chimes]

300
21:11.334 --> 21:12.543
[door keypad beeping]

301
21:12.668 --> 21:13.920
[error code beeps]

302
21:14.796 --> 21:16.464
[door keypad beeping]

303
21:16.589 --> 21:17.507
[error code beeps]

304
21:17.632 --> 21:19.550
[door keypad beeping]

305
21:19.675 --> 21:20.718
[error code beeps]

306
21:22.845 --> 21:23.763
What are you doing?

307
21:24.639 --> 21:25.681
Nothing works.

308
21:27.809 --> 21:30.812
I've tried your birthday, and your phone number too,

309
21:31.312 --> 21:33.981
the release of The 13th Season, and even your hire date.

310
21:34.649 --> 21:36.150
I don't even know my hire date.

311
21:37.193 --> 21:38.486
You're something else, huh?

312
21:39.028 --> 21:41.239
And you keep saying I know nothing about you.

313
21:48.162 --> 21:48.996
I'm hungry.

314
21:49.580 --> 21:50.873
Let me eat before I go.

315
21:58.798 --> 22:00.133
[gentle music concludes]

316
22:04.345 --> 22:05.471
When was my hire date?

317
22:05.596 --> 22:07.223
March 12th, 2018.

318
22:09.517 --> 22:11.144
Do you know which department I was in first?

319
22:11.269 --> 22:13.354
-Sales Division. -Are you a stalker or something?

320
22:16.315 --> 22:17.441
I heard it from Sang-hun.

321
22:18.609 --> 22:21.487
He said you're from Sales when I went to Sales regarding the survey.

322
22:22.572 --> 22:23.823
That's how I know.

323
22:27.660 --> 22:28.828
That's honest truth.

324
22:36.711 --> 22:41.632
And do you also know that I was an outcast there for a year?

325
22:44.427 --> 22:46.429
I was considered their star rookie.

326
22:48.055 --> 22:50.141
The Sales team took me under their wing

327
22:50.266 --> 22:52.101
and groomed me to be their star recruit.

328
22:55.188 --> 22:56.230
Two months into the job,

329
22:56.355 --> 22:58.774
I landed a retail deal and doubled our Sales.

330
22:58.900 --> 23:00.026
[soft music playing]

331
23:01.277 --> 23:02.653
I thought back then,

332
23:04.822 --> 23:06.908
at the very least, I'd become director.

333
23:09.869 --> 23:14.916
About six months into the job, we had team drinks with a buyer.

334
23:16.334 --> 23:19.212
and he gave little envelopes of cash to our team members.

335
23:22.048 --> 23:23.549
I said I was fine and refused.

336
23:24.800 --> 23:26.177
And starting the next day,

337
23:27.261 --> 23:29.513
things started happening that weren't so nice.

338
23:47.448 --> 23:49.033
Show me your finger.

339
24:12.682 --> 24:15.393
In that envelope, there was 300 grand.

340
24:16.769 --> 24:18.396
That was the amount of won in there.

341
24:20.898 --> 24:21.941
I was bitter.

342
24:23.609 --> 24:25.861
My conscience was worth 300 grand.

343
24:31.701 --> 24:35.246
That's why I'm going to sell it for a lot more.

344
24:37.498 --> 24:40.543
And well, do I still look wonderful to you?

345
24:44.505 --> 24:47.383
Su-a, you don't know me as well as you think.

346
24:48.801 --> 24:50.678
I'm not the person you imagine.

347
24:51.470 --> 24:52.722
Make sure you remember that.

348
24:53.055 --> 24:53.973
Also…

349
24:56.684 --> 24:58.185
there's no fantasy in this world.

350
25:08.696 --> 25:13.034
RAW MATERIAL MARGIN CALCULATION HUNMIN CONFECTIONERY

351
25:13.159 --> 25:15.077
SCANDAL CHART EXECUTIVE DIRECTOR YOON

352
25:23.502 --> 25:25.129
[Namgung] I'm not the person you imagine.

353
25:26.005 --> 25:27.214
Make sure you remember that.

354
25:27.631 --> 25:28.591
Also…

355
25:30.634 --> 25:32.261
there's no fantasy in this world.

356
25:33.387 --> 25:34.472
[soft music concludes]

357
25:34.597 --> 25:35.598
[Su-a sighs]

358
25:39.643 --> 25:40.811
Su-a, you want…

359
25:43.314 --> 25:44.523
Did she go shower?

360
25:45.441 --> 25:46.442
Huh.

361
25:47.485 --> 25:48.569
Um…

362
25:55.576 --> 25:57.244
[dramatic music playing]

363
26:01.624 --> 26:02.875
[dramatic music concludes]

364
26:03.751 --> 26:05.294
[news anchor] Rookie director Tak Se-yeong's film

365
26:05.419 --> 26:08.881
When I Woke Up in the Morning, I was a Dirt-Poor Job Seeker in Korea

366
26:09.548 --> 26:13.177
a.k.a Dirt-Poor Job Seeker, topped two million tickets

367
26:13.302 --> 26:15.846
in just two months, becoming this year's biggest hit…

368
26:16.680 --> 26:18.766
I checked the location you said you visited

369
26:18.891 --> 26:20.184
over the past four months.

370
26:21.060 --> 26:22.603
You weren't wandering at all.

371
26:22.728 --> 26:24.730
You were heading somewhere, so…

372
26:29.193 --> 26:32.446
Are there any particular moments that stand out of Myeong-dong at all?

373
26:36.283 --> 26:37.284
Are you listening at all?

374
26:38.077 --> 26:40.204
-Oh! -[diners gasp]

375
26:40.329 --> 26:41.163
I got it!

376
26:44.667 --> 26:47.503
[news anchor] …he's become he nation's most-watched rookie--

377
26:47.878 --> 26:49.505
-[exhales sharply] -[remote control thuds]

378
26:50.172 --> 26:54.301
Do you know what happens when the news talks about

379
26:54.427 --> 26:57.263
an amazing lawyer or someone winning a lawsuit?

380
26:57.888 --> 26:59.598
Something so annoying to me.

381
26:59.723 --> 27:00.808
Oh, so annoying.

382
27:03.102 --> 27:04.270
[exhales happily]

383
27:10.276 --> 27:11.277
Not smiling yet?

384
27:13.404 --> 27:14.321
[sighs]

385
27:16.532 --> 27:18.200
How can I get you to laugh?

386
27:22.246 --> 27:24.165
You don't know how much I love seeing you smile.

387
27:27.877 --> 27:30.045
-[chuckles softly] -["Striped Sweater" playing]

388
27:31.213 --> 27:33.549
TAGADA, WOLMIDO AMUSEMENT PARK

389
27:37.261 --> 27:38.262
[Tae-seung] Stop, stop, stop.

390
27:38.387 --> 27:41.348
Whoo!

391
27:43.225 --> 27:44.351
Wait, wait, wait, wait.

392
27:44.477 --> 27:46.395
[Mi-do cheers]

393
27:46.520 --> 27:47.938
You can get on now.

394
27:50.858 --> 27:51.734
You coming?

395
27:59.158 --> 28:00.784
Whoo!

396
28:06.665 --> 28:09.627
Whoo!

397
28:11.504 --> 28:13.255
[Tae-seung groans]

398
28:18.844 --> 28:21.597
I… can't ride anymore.

399
28:27.144 --> 28:28.521
Please don't.

400
28:29.897 --> 28:30.814
No way.

401
28:31.357 --> 28:32.399
I hate it.

402
28:33.108 --> 28:34.068
I'm done.

403
28:34.610 --> 28:35.819
I won't do it.

404
28:36.278 --> 28:39.198
You said you would do whatever it takes just to see me smile.

405
28:39.782 --> 28:40.616
[exhales deeply]

406
28:40.741 --> 28:46.247
Just to be clear, I never said I'd do anything.

407
28:48.958 --> 28:51.544
I asked what would make you smile, that's it.

408
28:55.798 --> 28:56.840
What if…

409
28:57.216 --> 28:58.175
Oh!

410
28:58.676 --> 28:59.552
Let's get something to eat.

411
29:00.427 --> 29:02.429
How about sashimi?

412
29:02.972 --> 29:03.889
Rockfish.

413
29:04.014 --> 29:05.599
Rockfish is great. You in?

414
29:06.475 --> 29:07.643
I'll go ride it alone.

415
29:08.018 --> 29:09.311
You go eat your rockfish.

416
29:10.271 --> 29:12.106
Wait a minute. Wait a minute!

417
29:14.692 --> 29:15.734
It's just…

418
29:16.402 --> 29:18.112
Isn't 12 times enough already?

419
29:19.196 --> 29:20.447
How many more rides do you--

420
29:20.573 --> 29:21.949
I can't shake the fear.

421
29:24.451 --> 29:27.204
After ten times, I usually feel okay.

422
29:27.746 --> 29:30.499
[sighs] Even though the fear doesn't go away.

423
29:38.340 --> 29:39.174
Okay.

424
29:42.177 --> 29:43.679
Let me just get some nausea pills.

425
29:52.021 --> 29:52.980
[chuckles softly]

426
30:01.822 --> 30:03.657
[cheers]

427
30:03.782 --> 30:05.117
Whoo!

428
30:06.076 --> 30:07.244
[laughs]

429
30:07.911 --> 30:10.372
Put your hands up. Whoo!

430
30:10.497 --> 30:13.375
-Whoo! [laughs] -Ah!

431
30:15.544 --> 30:17.004
-Ah!- -[Mi-do] Whoo!

432
30:17.838 --> 30:18.922
-Whoo! -Ah!

433
30:19.923 --> 30:21.175
[man] Hey, did you see that?

434
30:21.300 --> 30:22.134
What was it?

435
30:22.259 --> 30:23.302
When I Woke Up Today?

436
30:23.427 --> 30:24.261
HAEON HALL

437
30:24.386 --> 30:26.347
Uh, no, no, wait. Maybe When I Woke Up?

438
30:27.389 --> 30:29.141
Damn. What was that again?

439
30:29.642 --> 30:31.352
[woman] Oh, Dirt-Poor Job Seeker?

440
30:31.477 --> 30:32.603
[man] Oh, that's right.

441
30:32.728 --> 30:33.687
Is it a first-time director?

442
30:34.313 --> 30:36.273
Its mise-en-scene is better than Park Chan-wook's.

443
30:37.107 --> 30:38.817
Tak Jackson is a success.

444
30:41.987 --> 30:43.781
Hmm. College classmate.

445
30:45.949 --> 30:48.952
Hmm, that awkward nerd finally made it big.

446
30:49.078 --> 30:50.037
The irony.

447
30:51.455 --> 30:52.289
What should I do?

448
30:53.916 --> 30:56.210
Should I go and shut them all up?

449
30:56.669 --> 30:58.379
You wouldn't dare. I'm gonna kill you.

450
31:07.471 --> 31:08.555
[exhales sharply]

451
31:09.682 --> 31:11.600
I already told you about this once.

452
31:13.602 --> 31:15.938
If you feel embarrassed, to get back up.

453
31:19.525 --> 31:21.318
But the truth is, all I did was stand.

454
31:22.486 --> 31:24.113
I haven't taken a single step.

455
31:27.366 --> 31:29.493
I'm terrified of taking an unknown road.

456
31:33.956 --> 31:36.083
But most of all, I'm exhausted.

457
31:37.668 --> 31:38.585
Dedication.

458
31:38.711 --> 31:39.586
Energy.

459
31:40.587 --> 31:41.588
Those things are long gone.

460
31:42.464 --> 31:45.008
There's no courage in sight, let alone confidence.

461
31:47.678 --> 31:49.596
[tender music playing]

462
31:52.182 --> 31:54.393
Everyone around me is doing so well.

463
31:58.188 --> 32:00.524
It terrifies me that deep down I want to see

464
32:00.649 --> 32:02.776
all of them failing in everything they do.

465
32:04.862 --> 32:08.574
And that I'm too petty to even pretend to celebrate their success.

466
32:10.868 --> 32:14.371
I'm scared because I still doubt if the path I chose is right for me.

467
32:15.456 --> 32:19.001
But turning around now is even scarier.

468
32:20.794 --> 32:23.505
[breathes deeply]

469
32:26.175 --> 32:28.969
[fireworks bursting]

470
32:32.765 --> 32:35.142
If you think I'm pathetic, so be it.

471
32:36.769 --> 32:37.811
It's just…

472
32:38.729 --> 32:40.397
this is who I am now.

473
32:46.528 --> 32:47.571
[exhales]

474
32:51.867 --> 32:53.160
Oh, this isn't good.

475
32:56.497 --> 32:58.165
I think I like you even more now.

476
33:00.876 --> 33:01.877
[scoffs softly]

477
33:05.005 --> 33:05.839
Get up.

478
33:07.257 --> 33:10.636
I think I know exactly what it is you need.

479
33:14.264 --> 33:15.265
Trust me.

480
33:16.683 --> 33:17.559
Let's go.

481
33:20.312 --> 33:21.855
[exhales]

482
33:22.481 --> 33:23.649
This is supposed to help me?

483
33:23.774 --> 33:24.733
DIRT-POOR JOB SEEKER

484
33:24.858 --> 33:25.776
[Tae-seung] Yeah.

485
33:26.485 --> 33:28.362
You said you'd be scared to watch it alone.

486
33:29.404 --> 33:30.489
So now I'm watching it with you.

487
33:30.614 --> 33:31.824
[tender music concludes]

488
33:34.618 --> 33:36.411
We can leave anytime you want.

489
33:37.538 --> 33:38.914
Even just five minutes will do.

490
33:40.791 --> 33:42.709
You'll dump me when our month is over anyways.

491
33:44.670 --> 33:46.296
So who cares if you lose face with me?

492
33:46.964 --> 33:48.382
We won't see each other again.

493
33:48.715 --> 33:50.175
So why worry about pride?

494
33:50.634 --> 33:51.802
Don't talk about that.

495
33:52.553 --> 33:55.264
If you're really sorry, give me your hand.

496
33:58.809 --> 34:00.102
You'll be less scared if you do it.

497
34:00.227 --> 34:01.061
And…

498
34:01.562 --> 34:02.437
Hmm…

499
34:03.188 --> 34:04.106
I'll just hold you.

500
34:08.110 --> 34:09.069
[chuckles]

501
34:12.281 --> 34:15.534
[powerful classic music playing over speakers]

502
34:19.162 --> 34:20.789
[woman] I told you not to follow me.

503
34:22.833 --> 34:24.543
[man] I take back what I said.

504
34:28.255 --> 34:30.382
What is pathetic is not this planet,

505
34:32.926 --> 34:35.846
but me for running my mouth without knowing how you feel.

506
34:43.312 --> 34:44.479
Less scary with me, right?

507
34:47.316 --> 34:48.609
[music swells]

508
34:52.362 --> 34:53.655
[exhales deeply]

509
35:02.164 --> 35:04.291
How long do you want me to eat in silence, huh?

510
35:13.759 --> 35:15.302
Just don't let Sang-su catch you.

511
35:16.929 --> 35:17.930
He's a teenager.

512
35:18.430 --> 35:20.057
Even if he's chill like me,

513
35:20.182 --> 35:22.351
he inherited your tendency to hold grudges.

514
35:25.187 --> 35:26.813
It's not like it's a second wedding.

515
35:27.814 --> 35:29.441
Even if he finds out, he won't care.

516
35:29.566 --> 35:30.692
-[sobbing softly] -[Yeong-do] Hey.

517
35:32.903 --> 35:34.696
[somber instrumental music playing]

518
35:34.821 --> 35:36.281
[sobbing]

519
35:50.671 --> 35:51.713
I'm very happy.

520
35:53.048 --> 35:54.257
Don't flatter yourself.

521
35:55.258 --> 35:56.927
I'm not crying over you.

522
35:58.011 --> 36:00.263
[sobbing]

523
36:02.349 --> 36:03.642
What's going on with you?

524
36:05.102 --> 36:06.561
Why are you such a mess?

525
36:07.354 --> 36:08.230
Hey.

526
36:08.355 --> 36:11.400
I feel bad being the only one happy right now.

527
36:13.944 --> 36:15.112
I don't know.

528
36:15.988 --> 36:18.532
I thought I just wanted to brag to you.

529
36:19.783 --> 36:20.993
I guess it was a mistake.

530
36:23.120 --> 36:24.204
I guess…

531
36:26.498 --> 36:28.333
I wanted you to congratulate me.

532
36:36.758 --> 36:38.260
[somber instrumental music concludes]

533
36:45.642 --> 36:47.144
[exhales deeply]

534
36:47.686 --> 36:48.770
[door closes]

535
36:50.439 --> 36:52.941
"Midori4882" was you?

536
36:53.066 --> 36:54.401
[coughs]

537
36:54.526 --> 36:56.111
Get some fresh air in here.

538
36:56.236 --> 36:57.487
I'm allergic to cats.

539
36:59.573 --> 37:00.574
[scoffs]

540
37:03.160 --> 37:04.870
How did you find my post about Bambi?

541
37:05.245 --> 37:06.621
That's none of your business.

542
37:07.664 --> 37:10.042
I just came here to ask you three questions.

543
37:12.002 --> 37:13.754
I won't answer, whatever they are.

544
37:16.548 --> 37:18.842
Namgung did drag in school. I'll show you.

545
37:21.887 --> 37:22.846
[snickers]

546
37:24.514 --> 37:28.351
Number one, why did Namgung move to Procurement?

547
37:29.102 --> 37:31.438
Number two, who got disciplined

548
37:31.563 --> 37:33.523
for Namgung's mudflat accident?

549
37:33.648 --> 37:37.069
Number three, who drank with Namgung

550
37:37.986 --> 37:40.072
the night you stayed at his apartment?

551
37:41.823 --> 37:42.991
I'm not allowed to talk.

552
37:44.785 --> 37:46.203
He's really cute in drag.

553
37:49.539 --> 37:53.376
I'm curious, sure, but you have no right to know.

554
37:54.169 --> 37:57.130
The only reason you are doing this is to ease your guilt.

555
37:58.090 --> 37:59.674
Hmm. That's true.

556
38:00.801 --> 38:01.885
What's wrong with that?

557
38:02.344 --> 38:03.303
[scoffs]

558
38:03.887 --> 38:05.514
You really have no shame at all.

559
38:06.014 --> 38:06.848
That's it.

560
38:07.641 --> 38:10.143
I knew you had no shame when I saw you eat Coco Jelly.

561
38:11.394 --> 38:12.646
Why bring up Coco Jelly?

562
38:12.771 --> 38:16.233
Coco Jelly is a Happy Confectionery product.

563
38:17.317 --> 38:19.111
After his rice-cake chicken was ruined

564
38:19.236 --> 38:21.988
by Happy Confectionery, he never eats their products.

565
38:25.575 --> 38:28.453
I've only eaten Coco Jelly since middle school.

566
38:29.121 --> 38:30.956
They couldn't make a jelly better than Coco Jelly,

567
38:31.081 --> 38:32.582
so blame the Hunmin company then.

568
38:33.291 --> 38:36.128
If you're that mad, step up and make one yourself. How about that?

569
38:36.253 --> 38:38.213
The Candy Department handles jelly.

570
38:38.338 --> 38:39.214
I'm in Snacks.

571
38:40.048 --> 38:41.174
[exhales deeply]

572
38:41.299 --> 38:42.342
[scoffs]

573
38:46.596 --> 38:47.597
[huffs]

574
38:48.098 --> 38:49.182
I don't want to talk.

575
38:49.307 --> 38:50.308
Please leave.

576
39:05.740 --> 39:06.741
I was curious.

577
39:09.161 --> 39:10.245
I came for you.

578
39:10.495 --> 39:11.413
Why?

579
39:12.414 --> 39:13.707
Why are you curious about me?

580
39:14.332 --> 39:15.250
I wonder.

581
39:16.501 --> 39:18.128
Why am I so curious about you?

582
39:20.922 --> 39:21.882
[tense, upbeat music playing]

583
39:22.007 --> 39:25.677
Pulling a crazy stunt like this and coming all the way here.

584
39:31.600 --> 39:33.602
Why am I so curious about you?

585
39:40.358 --> 39:43.862
Let's say this is why I came today.

586
39:47.407 --> 39:48.992
Why did you take that? That's mine.

587
39:49.618 --> 39:51.244
No, it's not. It's mine.

588
39:51.912 --> 39:53.997
Namgung drew this, so the drawing is his.

589
39:54.122 --> 39:56.583
And what's his is mine, so this is mine, too.

590
39:58.376 --> 39:59.211
It's mine.

591
39:59.336 --> 40:00.212
He drew it, yeah.

592
40:00.337 --> 40:02.214
He gifted it to me, so it's not yours.

593
40:04.174 --> 40:06.092
[both breathing heavily]

594
40:10.096 --> 40:10.931
[Su-a] Give it back!

595
40:11.056 --> 40:13.183
-[Mi-do] Let go! -[Su-a] It's mine, give it back!

596
40:13.308 --> 40:14.351
[Mi-do] Ah, shit!

597
40:14.684 --> 40:15.894
[both grunting]

598
40:16.019 --> 40:17.103
[Mi-do] Let go!

599
40:18.063 --> 40:19.397
-[Su-a] Hey! -[Mi-do grunts]

600
40:19.981 --> 40:20.982
[Su-a] Hey!

601
40:21.608 --> 40:22.901
[Mi-do] Hey! [grunts]

602
40:23.485 --> 40:24.444
[Su-a] Give it to me!

603
40:24.569 --> 40:25.904
[Mi-do] I said it's mine!

604
40:26.446 --> 40:27.364
[grunts]

605
40:27.489 --> 40:28.573
[Su-a shrieks]

606
40:29.199 --> 40:31.743
[both panting]

607
40:34.120 --> 40:35.664
[tense, upbeat music concludes]

608
40:35.789 --> 40:37.540
Are you insane? What is this even--

609
40:42.587 --> 40:43.588
[Mi-do] Can't you…

610
40:45.757 --> 40:47.175
just give it to me?

611
40:48.760 --> 40:50.387
I know I have no right over it.

612
40:52.222 --> 40:54.015
And I know I have no shame.

613
40:58.979 --> 41:00.438
Can I please just have it?

614
41:02.983 --> 41:04.192
[tender music playing]

615
41:05.860 --> 41:07.821
I've been looking for it forever.

616
41:09.906 --> 41:12.200
You have no idea how much I wanted it.

617
41:16.913 --> 41:17.914
So please…

618
41:19.416 --> 41:20.417
can I have it?

619
41:29.509 --> 41:30.635
[tender music concludes]

620
41:34.889 --> 41:36.683
[Mi-do] I've been looking for it forever.

621
41:38.018 --> 41:39.811
You have no idea how much I wanted it.

622
41:42.188 --> 41:43.106
[Sang-hun] Huge news!

623
41:44.190 --> 41:45.734
Manager Jeong lost it yesterday.

624
41:45.859 --> 41:47.319
Come on, that's not huge news.

625
41:47.694 --> 41:50.280
He causes trouble every other day, we all know that.

626
41:50.405 --> 41:51.364
Mm-hmm.

627
41:51.489 --> 41:52.949
Tougher than the ones he's used to.

628
41:53.408 --> 41:56.244
He got drunk with a client and clocked him right in the jaw.

629
41:56.619 --> 41:57.454
[scoffs]

630
41:57.579 --> 41:58.663
Serves him right.

631
41:59.205 --> 42:00.749
I hope he gets sued for that.

632
42:00.874 --> 42:02.834
Mr. Namgung went to beg on his knees.

633
42:03.168 --> 42:04.586
They're making major legal threats.

634
42:05.378 --> 42:06.254
What?

635
42:08.173 --> 42:09.632
Yeah, he's there right now.

636
42:10.800 --> 42:11.760
[sighs]

637
42:17.849 --> 42:19.017
[groans]

638
42:19.642 --> 42:21.561
This is attempted murder.

639
42:21.978 --> 42:23.521
Got it? [yelps]

640
42:23.897 --> 42:24.898
DAEPYEONG MILLING

641
42:25.065 --> 42:26.024
Forget that.

642
42:26.149 --> 42:28.860
Rewrite the contract with a 15% increase.

643
42:29.444 --> 42:34.032
Oh, and by the way, don't even think about getting on your knees.

644
42:34.532 --> 42:36.951
I don't even have a drop of sympathy for that.

645
42:37.202 --> 42:38.745
Understood?! [yelps]

646
42:40.205 --> 42:41.581
I'm not about to get on my knees.

647
42:43.541 --> 42:45.001
I can't stand embarrassment.

648
42:53.218 --> 42:54.886
Nice nameplate you got there.

649
42:55.011 --> 42:56.304
CEO CHOI YEONG-DO

650
42:58.598 --> 43:00.183
[spirited music playing]

651
43:02.727 --> 43:04.896
[Mr. Choi] Hey! What are you-- What are you doing? Stop! No, no, no!

652
43:05.021 --> 43:06.773
Stop, stop, stop, stop! No, no, no. No, no, no. Stop!

653
43:06.898 --> 43:08.274
-[object clatters] -[Mr. Choi] No!

654
43:09.401 --> 43:10.360
[employees gasp]

655
43:13.196 --> 43:14.906
Apparently, CEO Choi was really mad.

656
43:18.993 --> 43:20.412
Are you okay, sir?

657
43:20.995 --> 43:21.913
Thank you.

658
43:22.747 --> 43:24.666
You asshole! Are you mad?

659
43:24.791 --> 43:25.917
You're bleeding!

660
43:27.043 --> 43:27.919
You're insane!

661
43:28.628 --> 43:29.671
I'm fine, sir.

662
43:30.255 --> 43:31.798
If this helps soothe your temper,

663
43:31.923 --> 43:33.550
I'll take whatever hits you throw at me.

664
43:33.675 --> 43:35.260
-[quivers] -[employees whispering]

665
43:35.385 --> 43:36.428
Did you see that?

666
43:37.512 --> 43:38.513
Okay, no.

667
43:39.305 --> 43:40.723
That's not true. [laughs nervously]

668
43:41.599 --> 43:42.934
I swear I didn't throw that!

669
43:43.059 --> 43:44.811
Let's call it even for yesterday's assault.

670
43:46.771 --> 43:48.273
I'll see you at the next meeting.

671
43:57.240 --> 43:58.241
[spirited music concludes]

672
44:01.077 --> 44:02.078
Told you, right?

673
44:03.371 --> 44:04.372
What's wrong with him?

674
44:05.582 --> 44:06.499
[gasps]

675
44:08.793 --> 44:10.044
[phone vibrates]

676
44:15.884 --> 44:17.218
MANAGER EOM HO-SIK

677
44:17.343 --> 44:20.263
PROCUREMENT NEVER RESTS YOU DIDN'T MESS UP TOO, RIGHT?

678
44:31.608 --> 44:34.694
Is it right for a manager to slack off in broad daylight?

679
44:35.862 --> 44:40.033
With a six-month pay cut and being passed on for promotion,

680
44:40.158 --> 44:41.493
I've earned some slacking off.

681
44:43.578 --> 44:44.746
Ah, shit.

682
44:45.872 --> 44:47.874
If only I hadn't lost that phone.

683
44:49.417 --> 44:51.085
I caught them red-handed.

684
44:52.420 --> 44:54.172
Hey, that cell phone.

685
44:54.714 --> 44:55.673
Did you really not take it?

686
44:56.216 --> 44:58.176
Whoever stole your phone were professionals.

687
44:59.886 --> 45:02.472
It was probably pawned and shipped across the Pacific.

688
45:02.805 --> 45:05.266
Nah, I'm sure it's still in Korea.

689
45:06.309 --> 45:10.021
Even if I have to search every pawn shop, I'll definitely find it.

690
45:15.610 --> 45:17.320
You should change your mind while you can.

691
45:18.780 --> 45:21.449
I don't know why you suddenly want to play the hero.

692
45:22.575 --> 45:24.244
Just be a hero for Su-min, okay?

693
45:26.162 --> 45:27.288
Su-min, my daughter,

694
45:28.373 --> 45:30.625
went to the International Luce Piano Contest.

695
45:31.167 --> 45:32.043
[chuckles]

696
45:32.168 --> 45:33.211
Pretty hard to say.

697
45:34.087 --> 45:35.380
She made it to finals again.

698
45:37.298 --> 45:39.384
That's why I gotta make director.

699
45:39.926 --> 45:41.719
If I'm not, I can't support her.

700
45:42.845 --> 45:44.138
So I'll make director.

701
45:46.516 --> 45:47.767
That's beyond what I can do.

702
45:49.519 --> 45:52.355
I thought that material disposal audit made my position

703
45:52.480 --> 45:53.523
clear enough to you.

704
45:55.942 --> 45:58.403
I know you did that on purpose to stop me.

705
46:04.117 --> 46:04.993
You're wrong.

706
46:05.285 --> 46:06.828
I did it to impress Procurement.

707
46:10.582 --> 46:13.251
Their approval would make you happy?

708
46:15.420 --> 46:17.046
I didn't ask you to come join in.

709
46:18.131 --> 46:21.718
I called you to stop you from doing what you're doing.

710
46:24.512 --> 46:25.722
[door bell tinkles]

711
46:26.931 --> 46:28.057
The next batter's up.

712
46:30.852 --> 46:31.769
I'll get going.

713
46:40.278 --> 46:42.196
PRIME ON CONVENIENCE STORE

714
46:44.324 --> 46:46.326
I touched it earlier and it opened up.

715
46:53.916 --> 46:54.876
It's only two stitches.

716
46:57.670 --> 46:58.796
They said it won't scar.

717
46:59.756 --> 47:00.673
Just transfer out.

718
47:03.301 --> 47:05.386
I can't get you back on the TF team this year,

719
47:06.179 --> 47:07.847
unless we find Manager Eom's phone.

720
47:10.099 --> 47:13.144
There are more files to investigate, so request a transfer.

721
47:13.269 --> 47:14.604
I ain't gonna do it.

722
47:14.729 --> 47:16.022
It's too much trouble.

723
47:20.735 --> 47:21.861
It's for Mi-do, right?

724
47:23.071 --> 47:27.033
The reason you live like this, enduring this misery day after day.

725
47:28.826 --> 47:30.036
All for Mi-do, right?

726
47:31.537 --> 47:32.914
[soft, emotional music playing]

727
47:35.667 --> 47:37.669
And why are you bringing her up now?

728
47:38.586 --> 47:40.421
Because Lee Mi-do is the brake on your life.

729
47:42.465 --> 47:44.092
You're stopping the investigation

730
47:44.217 --> 47:47.845
and swallowing all this humiliation in Procurement, and…

731
47:50.682 --> 47:52.266
even dating me without feeling it.

732
47:54.477 --> 47:55.978
It was all for Mi-do, right?

733
48:00.608 --> 48:01.984
Does she even know?

734
48:03.945 --> 48:06.197
That deep down you're dying inside because of her?

735
48:06.531 --> 48:07.740
That you've lost all your color?

736
48:08.116 --> 48:09.117
Does she have any idea?

737
48:09.742 --> 48:12.203
Su-a, enough. You've gone too far.

738
48:12.328 --> 48:13.788
Then I'll go even further.

739
48:15.581 --> 48:17.959
You have nothing in your life without Mi-do, right?

740
48:19.585 --> 48:20.712
You're just hollow.

741
48:23.172 --> 48:24.382
Please don't live like that.

742
48:25.299 --> 48:28.970
An empty life all for Mi-do, with nothing of your own.

743
48:30.304 --> 48:31.472
Don't live like that.

744
48:40.356 --> 48:41.274
[door bell tinkles]

745
48:41.399 --> 48:43.359
[soft, emotional music concludes]

746
48:50.324 --> 48:51.617
Repeat what you said.

747
48:53.244 --> 48:54.454
Say it again.

748
48:55.371 --> 48:56.456
Let me hear it.

749
48:59.751 --> 49:02.253
Like I said, nothing in your life without Mi-do, right?

750
49:03.921 --> 49:05.047
That you're hollow.

751
49:10.845 --> 49:11.763
[exhales sharply]

752
49:16.851 --> 49:17.852
[tender music playing]

753
49:17.977 --> 49:18.936
[Namgung] You're right.

754
49:20.688 --> 49:21.981
Mi-do is everything to me.

755
49:23.983 --> 49:27.904
And I'm certain I'm willing to do anything for my everything.

756
49:30.740 --> 49:32.366
Even if she loves another man?

757
49:35.536 --> 49:37.079
And she leaves you for that guy?

758
49:37.205 --> 49:38.080
Yes.

759
49:38.873 --> 49:40.041
I'll wait for her.

760
49:41.000 --> 49:42.376
Because I know she'll return.

761
49:44.837 --> 49:45.755
You know?

762
49:47.256 --> 49:48.633
Even if she doesn't, it's fine.

763
49:50.051 --> 49:52.094
Like you mentioned, without Mi-do, I'm nothing.

764
49:53.471 --> 49:56.808
Without her, I wouldn't even be here to begin with.

765
49:56.933 --> 50:00.269
So now, don't act like you know anything about me.

766
50:01.229 --> 50:03.648
My life is shitty enough, so don't you dare pity me.

767
50:13.991 --> 50:15.076
Are you disappointed?

768
50:17.245 --> 50:18.079
Yeah.

769
50:19.789 --> 50:20.915
I am a lot.

770
50:21.040 --> 50:22.291
[music softens]

771
50:23.209 --> 50:24.293
Even though…

772
50:26.671 --> 50:28.756
I still think you're a wonderful guy.

773
50:30.550 --> 50:32.635
Watching how much you can love someone else…

774
50:34.345 --> 50:35.930
it's so frustrating.

775
50:37.348 --> 50:38.641
It makes me so mad.

776
50:41.686 --> 50:43.145
Yet, you're an amazing guy.

777
50:46.440 --> 50:47.900
You're absolutely wonderful.

778
50:59.787 --> 51:01.289
[sobs softly]

779
51:11.090 --> 51:12.675
[music swells]

780
51:18.139 --> 51:21.726
50 GOOD THINGS ABOUT NAMGUNG HO 1. HE TAKES CHARGE AND FIXES EVERY CRISIS

781
51:43.664 --> 51:44.999
[tender music concludes]

782
51:48.502 --> 51:49.879
Do you hate that she's remarrying?

783
51:50.004 --> 51:50.880
Hey, shush.

784
51:51.172 --> 51:52.256
Sang-su can hear you.

785
51:53.090 --> 51:54.050
He already knows.

786
51:55.885 --> 51:56.719
Huh?

787
51:58.429 --> 51:59.263
And you?

788
52:04.477 --> 52:05.645
[Wan-do exhales sharply]

789
52:13.945 --> 52:17.114
Honestly, I thought I was a cool enough ex-husband.

790
52:18.282 --> 52:21.702
And I couldn't even congratulate her at all. [laughs]

791
52:22.620 --> 52:23.955
Man. [laughs]

792
52:24.080 --> 52:25.456
Then go try and get her back.

793
52:30.753 --> 52:32.463
What? You still love her, don't you?

794
52:33.422 --> 52:34.465
Go get her back.

795
52:36.008 --> 52:36.968
[Yeong-do] Oh, come on.

796
52:37.843 --> 52:38.886
Are you crazy?

797
52:41.013 --> 52:42.098
[Namgung] Can't be helped.

798
52:42.807 --> 52:43.724
Don't worry about it.

799
52:45.184 --> 52:46.519
Just take good care of your wife.

800
52:48.020 --> 52:48.896
Yeah.

801
52:49.021 --> 52:49.939
[call drops]

802
53:01.867 --> 53:02.910
[exhales shakily]

803
53:04.370 --> 53:05.997
Don't make an excuse that you fell.

804
53:06.706 --> 53:07.873
Why are you hurt, huh?

805
53:10.001 --> 53:10.960
Don't sweat it.

806
53:11.210 --> 53:12.086
Just forget it.

807
53:23.723 --> 53:24.932
Something up with you?

808
53:28.436 --> 53:29.395
Because of that guy?

809
53:38.654 --> 53:39.822
You like her, don't you?

810
53:42.324 --> 53:43.200
[scoffs softly]

811
53:45.077 --> 53:45.911
Park Su-a.

812
53:47.580 --> 53:48.789
You like her, don't you?

813
53:49.540 --> 53:50.958
What's making you ask that?

814
53:51.709 --> 53:53.002
Hey, why do you think I'm…

815
53:57.256 --> 53:58.424
Forget it. Don't care.

816
54:00.051 --> 54:01.594
Don't tell Yeong-do or Wan-do.

817
54:02.219 --> 54:03.512
They'll only worry about it.

818
54:06.057 --> 54:06.932
Stop liking her.

819
54:08.434 --> 54:10.102
[sentimental music playing]

820
54:10.227 --> 54:12.688
[breathing deeply]

821
54:18.569 --> 54:20.780
Just stop liking her, okay?

822
54:36.295 --> 54:37.880
Wake me up at 9:00 a.m.

823
54:38.380 --> 54:39.256
I don't want to miss this.

824
54:42.259 --> 54:44.637
[Wan-do] I don't want you to regret it like I do.

825
54:47.723 --> 54:48.557
You know it.

826
54:49.308 --> 54:50.434
Everything I did.

827
54:52.686 --> 54:53.729
That hurt Bo-ra.

828
54:55.022 --> 54:55.898
I know.

829
54:57.900 --> 54:59.068
Stop worrying and rest.

830
55:07.284 --> 55:09.578
-[sentimental music concludes] -[dog barking in distance]

831
55:17.920 --> 55:20.339
QUEENS HAIR SALON

832
55:21.674 --> 55:23.592
[Ho-sik] Su-a caught the kid who stole my phone.

833
55:24.468 --> 55:26.679
She found the pawn shop and is on her way there.

834
55:27.388 --> 55:29.723
My wife's appendix burst, so I can't go.

835
55:30.391 --> 55:33.018
You know, gangs run places like that, so it's dangerous.

836
55:33.686 --> 55:34.645
Please go check on her.

837
55:35.229 --> 55:36.605
Su-a won't listen to me.

838
55:39.191 --> 55:40.901
["Day and Night" playing]

839
55:52.204 --> 55:54.290
-[tires screeching] -[car horn honking]

840
56:18.731 --> 56:20.191
A pirate ship.

841
56:22.234 --> 56:23.944
I want to ride that one next.

842
56:31.535 --> 56:32.995
[tires screech]

843
56:47.468 --> 56:48.427
[gasps]

844
56:48.552 --> 56:49.678
[tires screech]

845
56:57.269 --> 57:00.147
[GPS] You have left the route. Recalculating.

846
57:13.327 --> 57:14.203
[Mi-do] Su-a.

847
57:15.162 --> 57:16.330
You like her, don't you?

848
57:18.207 --> 57:19.333
[Su-a] Mr. Namgung.

849
57:20.793 --> 57:22.378
I want to make you happy.

850
57:23.629 --> 57:25.214
Every single second.

851
57:26.090 --> 57:27.258
While we're dating.

852
57:30.010 --> 57:32.263
Not just for a second, like I said before.

853
57:35.140 --> 57:36.642
That's my only goal.

854
58:03.752 --> 58:05.004
You get that old lady's money?

855
58:05.129 --> 58:06.046
[man] Oh, right.

856
58:06.171 --> 58:07.089
Shit.

857
58:09.758 --> 58:10.884
[song concludes]

858
58:11.010 --> 58:12.636
I got caught red-handed.

859
58:13.512 --> 58:17.349
I don't think she's an officer, but she's crazy.

860
58:18.058 --> 58:18.892
[sighs]

861
58:19.018 --> 58:20.060
FRIENDLY DAILY LOANS

862
58:20.269 --> 58:21.520
I'll make this quick.

863
58:22.479 --> 58:24.690
April 22nd, 7:22.

864
58:25.357 --> 58:27.860
Outside exit one of Sindaebang, a man in his fifties.

865
58:28.694 --> 58:29.737
Waiting for a driver.

866
58:30.446 --> 58:32.323
You stole the phone of that man, right?

867
58:33.157 --> 58:34.116
Give it back now.

868
58:34.867 --> 58:35.743
[chuckles]

869
58:37.786 --> 58:39.038
This girl's got no fear.

870
58:39.455 --> 58:40.581
To catch this punk thief,

871
58:40.706 --> 58:42.916
I stayed up three nights stalking Sindaebang Station,

872
58:43.375 --> 58:45.127
so I have no sense of fear at this point.

873
58:45.836 --> 58:48.464
Return the phone now, and I'll leave quietly.

874
58:49.089 --> 58:54.428
Cutie, once you set foot in here, quietly is not in your cards.

875
59:01.226 --> 59:02.311
[tense music building]

876
59:02.436 --> 59:05.439
Ah, I had a good hand too.

877
59:12.112 --> 59:14.990
[panting]

878
59:34.259 --> 59:35.260
[emergency services] Hello?

879
59:35.969 --> 59:37.012
Please go ahead.

880
59:37.388 --> 59:39.139
Do you hear me? Are you in danger?

881
59:39.723 --> 59:40.641
Oh…

882
59:40.766 --> 59:42.351
[music rises]

883
59:49.858 --> 59:51.193
[tense music fades]

884
59:57.699 --> 59:59.576
[man, over recording] Hello? Please go ahead.

885
01:00:00.369 --> 01:00:01.787
Do you hear me? Are you in danger?

886
01:00:02.371 --> 01:00:03.914
Good thing I had that ready.

887
01:00:13.424 --> 01:00:14.550
Oh yes, hello?

888
01:00:15.300 --> 01:00:17.803
There's a pawn shop that fences stolen phones.

889
01:00:18.679 --> 01:00:19.763
I have evidence.

890
01:00:20.305 --> 01:00:21.515
[footsteps approaching rapidly]

891
01:00:21.640 --> 01:00:23.308
The location of the place is…

892
01:00:30.482 --> 01:00:31.733
[panting]

893
01:00:31.859 --> 01:00:33.110
[tender music playing]

894
01:00:43.328 --> 01:00:44.705
[sobs softly]

895
01:00:49.126 --> 01:00:50.294
Are you that frightened?

896
01:00:54.548 --> 01:00:56.550
Are you so afraid of Namgung…

897
01:00:58.552 --> 01:00:59.511
liking her?

898
01:01:11.356 --> 01:01:13.484
What can I do so you don't hurt?

899
01:01:23.035 --> 01:01:24.745
What if you try to like me more?

900
01:01:27.831 --> 01:01:29.208
More than Namgung.

901
01:01:31.793 --> 01:01:33.420
Try to like me more.

902
01:01:40.469 --> 01:01:41.720
I'll treat you right.

903
01:01:53.774 --> 01:01:54.942
Please give me a chance.

904
01:02:20.759 --> 01:02:22.970
[panting]

905
01:02:33.105 --> 01:02:34.815
[music swells]

906
01:02:42.864 --> 01:02:43.782
[music softens]

907
01:02:52.374 --> 01:02:54.251
A LOVE OTHER THAN YOURS

908
01:02:58.088 --> 01:02:59.881
[sweet Korean pop song playing]

909
01:03:01.383 --> 01:03:03.885
SAMHWA MOVIES

910
01:03:05.387 --> 01:03:08.056
50 GOOD THINGS ABOUT NAMGUNG HO

911
01:03:09.391 --> 01:03:10.475
[Namgung] Who was it?

912
01:03:10.601 --> 01:03:11.685
Who took your files?

913
01:03:11.810 --> 01:03:13.687
[Su-a] You'll get in trouble if you stay involved.

914
01:03:13.812 --> 01:03:15.480
[Tae-seung] Why can't you give in just this once?

915
01:03:15.606 --> 01:03:17.274
[Mi-do] I'm the one who gives in to you.

916
01:03:17.399 --> 01:03:20.777
You tore open my deepest wound, and I'm still seeing you.

917
01:03:20.902 --> 01:03:21.945
Hilarious.

918
01:03:22.070 --> 01:03:23.530
Mi-do is really giving in.

919
01:03:23.655 --> 01:03:25.866
[Tae-sung] All I want to do is forget about you.

920
01:03:25.991 --> 01:03:26.825
Got that?

921
01:03:26.950 --> 01:03:28.869
[Mi-do] Then let's both try hard to forget.

922
01:03:28.994 --> 01:03:31.413
I take back telling you to stop liking her.

923
01:03:32.122 --> 01:03:33.248
I regret it.

924
01:03:36.752 --> 01:03:37.794
[sweet Korean pop song concludes]
